# Compile before pull requests

`make` / `make all` builds only the main XCSoar binary. Include-order and
header collisions often fail only in debug tools (`RunMapWindow` and other
`Run*` programs in `build/test.mk`).

Before creating or submitting a PR, compile the full tree on UNIX:

```bash
make -j$(nproc) TARGET=UNIX USE_CCACHE=y everything
```

`everything` builds the main binary plus optional outputs, `debug` (`Run*`
tools), unit-test binaries, and `build-harness`. A successful main-binary
build is not enough.

When the change includes UI-free logic, prefer `everything check`.

`WERROR=y` is already the default when `DEBUG=y`. Details:
`docs/content/en/5.dev/01.build.md`.
